# --- Python (backend/) ---
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
*.egg-info/

# --- Node (frontend/) ---
node_modules/
dist/
*.local

# --- Env files (never commit real secrets; .env.example is tracked) ---
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# --- macOS ---
.DS_Store

# --- Verify receipts: TRACKED, deliberately ---
# These were ignored from the T-0 skeleton commit onward, as "hook-generated
# verify receipts" -- i.e. build artifacts. That stopped being true once
# harness-protocol.md made ticket status DERIVED from them ("receipt in
# .claude/evidence/ = resolved"). Ignored receipts mean status is derived from
# one laptop's filesystem: a fresh clone, CI, or a reviewer sees zero receipts
# and reads every ticket as unstarted, and verify_submission.sh's freshness
# gate fails on their machine for reasons that have nothing to do with the
# code. The asymmetry was the giveaway -- .claude/evidence-v1/ was tracked all
# along, so the OLD receipts shipped and the new ones did not.
# Decision 2026-08-15: track them. Cost accepted: receipts churn on every close
# and can conflict across parallel worktrees.

# --- Submission build artifact (T-13) ---
# submission/build_zip.sh regenerates this from scratch, and
# scripts/verify_submission.sh rebuilds it fresh on every run, so the zip is a
# derived artifact -- committing it would churn 1.6MB of binary in every diff
# for no gain. The script that builds it IS tracked.
submission/*.zip

# --- Per-session ticket claims (T-21) ---
# .claude/claims/<session_id> is machine-local, disposable ownership state:
# it names a Claude Code session that does not exist in any other checkout.
# .claude/active-ticket stays TRACKED -- it is the human-visible marker of
# which ticket is in flight.
.claude/claims/

# --- Runtime output (T-26) ---
# jarvis.pipeline.latency.LatencyLogger's DEFAULT_LATENCY_LOG_PATH is the
# relative path "var/latency.jsonl", written wherever a run's cwd happens to
# be (backend/var/ for a local `uv run` from backend/); no leading slash so
# this also covers a top-level var/ if some other entrypoint's cwd is the
# repo root. Per-run telemetry, not something to diff or ship in a
# submission zip -- see docs/latency-report.md for where the durable,
# committed measurement history actually lives.
var/
